meta {
  name: 03_KeyRoleFilter
  seq: 3
}

docs {
  Scenario: The key role party filter controls whether the subject's key role parties are returned

    Given a service owner lists the daily leader of an accounting firm, whose clients are
    reached through the firm's key role
    When key role parties are included, the clients are in the list
    When key role parties are excluded, those clients drop out, while the firm itself and a
    party that delegated directly to the person stay

  This folder covers only includePartiesViaKeyRoles, which the service applies deterministically.
  includeSubParties and includeInactiveParties are left for a later slice: the subunit filter
  is a known defect (#3522, the filter is resolved but never applied) and the inactive window
  is already covered by 09_DeletedParties.
}
